# The operator's declared kube-context for scripts/lib/require-cluster.sh.
# LOCAL ON PURPOSE, NOT COMMITTED. Baking one lab's context name into a chart
# other people deploy would make the guard wrong for every one of them, and a
# guard that is wrong by default is a guard they delete. A fresh clone has no
# declaration and every cluster-touching script refuses until someone states
# which cluster they mean -- which is the safe direction, and the point.
.expected-context
